{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wa32P1AA3GFA9rgsp63Ypa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"node:test runner\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"node:test runner - Visual Studio Marketplace\",\"url\":\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=connor4312.nodejs-testing\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js node:test module\",\"url\":\"https://bun.com/reference/node/test\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js Test Runner\",\"url\":\"https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/nodejs_test_runner.asp\"},{\"title\":\"Test runner\",\"url\":\"https://nodejs.org/docs/latest-v24.x/api/test.html\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring the Node.js native test runner - LogRocket Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.logrocket.com/exploring-node-js-native-test-runner/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use the Node.js Native Test Runner (node --test)\",\"url\":\"https://blog.appsignal.com/2024/07/17/exploring-the-nodejs-native-test-runner.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - rtfeldman/node-test-runner: Runs elm-test suites from Node.js. Get it with npm install -g elm-test · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rtfeldman/node-test-runner\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use Node.js Test Runner: A Detailed Guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.testmuai.com/blog/nodejs-test-runner/\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js Built-in Test Runner (node:test): Complete Guide for 2026\",\"url\":\"https://qaskills.sh/blog/node-test-runner-built-in-guide-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what you need to know about the node:test runner:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe 'node:test' module is Node.js's built-in test runner that provides a zero-dependency testing framework. It was introduced as a stable API in Node.js 20 and is designed to be a fast, modern alternative to external testing frameworks.\n\n## Key Features\n\nIt supports test() functions, lifecycle hooks (before, after), and assertions. Tests run in isolation with concurrent support, snapshot testing, and detailed reporting, making it a lightweight alternative to external test frameworks.\n\nThe test runner offers zero configuration (works out of the box), native ESM and CommonJS compatibility, parallel execution by default, and test isolation with each test running in its own context.\n\n## Running Tests\n\nThe node:test module is accompanied by the Node.js test runner which is accessible through the node --test command. The runner automatically locates and executes tests from files ending in .test.{js,mjs,cjs}, -test.{js,mjs,cjs}, and \\_test.{js,mjs,cjs} in any directory.\n\n## VS Code Integration\n\nThere's also a VS Code extension that provides test integration for node:test native tests.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ae7788e-26e2-4840-b44f-4a4df2108262","uuid":"37ff600a-0f3d-4c3b-b619-d1c0215b95c6","timestamp":"2026-10-05T03:52:55.608Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"node:test runner","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014Uf2fhvAw2FrKktFfvFAJt","content":[{"title":"node:test runner - Visual Studio Marketplace","url":"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=connor4312.nodejs-testing"},{"title":"Node.js node:test module","url":"https://bun.com/reference/node/test"},{"title":"Node.js Test Runner","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/nodejs_test_runner.asp"},{"title":"Test runner","url":"https://nodejs.org/docs/latest-v24.x/api/test.html"},{"title":"Exploring the Node.js native test runner - LogRocket Blog","url":"https://blog.logrocket.com/exploring-node-js-native-test-runner/"},{"title":"How to Use the Node.js Native Test Runner (node --test)","url":"https://blog.appsignal.com/2024/07/17/exploring-the-nodejs-native-test-runner.html"},{"title":"GitHub - rtfeldman/node-test-runner: Runs elm-test suites from Node.js. Get it with npm install -g elm-test · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/rtfeldman/node-test-runner"},{"title":"How to Use Node.js Test Runner: A Detailed Guide","url":"https://www.testmuai.com/blog/nodejs-test-runner/"},{"title":"Node.js Built-in Test Runner (node:test): Complete Guide for 2026","url":"https://qaskills.sh/blog/node-test-runner-built-in-guide-2026"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what you need to know about the node:test runner:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe 'node:test' module is Node.js's built-in test runner that provides a zero-dependency testing framework. It was introduced as a stable API in Node.js 20 and is designed to be a fast, modern alternative to external testing frameworks.\n\n## Key Features\n\nIt supports test() functions, lifecycle hooks (before, after), and assertions. Tests run in isolation with concurrent support, snapshot testing, and detailed reporting, making it a lightweight alternative to external test frameworks.\n\nThe test runner offers zero configuration (works out of the box), native ESM and CommonJS compatibility, parallel execution by default, and test isolation with each test running in its own context.\n\n## Running Tests\n\nThe node:test module is accompanied by the Node.js test runner which is accessible through the node --test command. The runner automatically locates and executes tests from files ending in .test.{js,mjs,cjs}, -test.{js,mjs,cjs}, and \\_test.{js,mjs,cjs} in any directory.\n\n## VS Code Integration\n\nThere's also a VS Code extension that provides test integration for node:test native tests."],"durationSeconds":6.4229231,"searchCount":1}}
